---
description: How to work with, and change, this project's fail-closed Cursor hooks
globs: ".cursor/hooks.json,.cursor/hooks/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

These files are the project's guard rails. Change them only when the human asks for that exact change.

- Permission hooks (`beforeShellExecution`, `beforeReadFile`, `beforeMCPExecution`, `preToolUse`, `subagentStart`)
  must keep `"failClosed": true`. Without it, a crash, timeout or exit code other than 2 lets the action through.
- Project hooks run from the project root: commands are `python3 .cursor/hooks/<script>.py`, never `./hooks/...`.
- `beforeMCPExecution` doesn't run in cloud agents. Keep the `preToolUse` hook with matcher `^MCP:` next to it.
- `preToolUse` doesn't enforce `"ask"`, so tools that need approval are denied there.
- Matchers are regexes. Test new ones.
- A permission hook that prints invalid JSON blocks the action. Print exactly one JSON object.
- Every new rule needs a deny case and an allow case in `selftest.py`. Run `hooks_check.py` and `selftest.py` after
  any change.
